## Field manual (field_manual)
fictoria.manual.title=§0§lNew Player Guide
fictoria.manual.index_body=Pick a chapter to read.\n§7Right-click this guide in your hand to come back at any time.§r
fictoria.manual.close=§8Close
fictoria.manual.back=§eBack to contents
fictoria.manual.ch1.title=§lChapter 1  From the First Life
fictoria.manual.ch1.body=§eHow to get one?§r\n· Creative mode:\n· The "Gear → Tactical Items" tab holds filled Phantoria Balls and every module; spawn eggs are on the "Items" page.\n· Hold a filled Phantoria Ball and right-click a block → she appears at once.\n· Survival mode:\n· Craft "Heart / Card_1" to tame her: place 3 emeralds diagonally in a crafting table, then hold and right-click to finish taming.\n· Craft an "Empty Phantoria Ball" to store and release maids like a Poké Ball: 8 emeralds in a ring with a card in the middle.\n\nAs a new player, your first entry into this world automatically grants you a Phantoria Ball with a maid inside, plus this guide.
fictoria.manual.ch2.title=§lChapter 2  Ordinary Maid
fictoria.manual.ch2.body=She is an ordinary maid when first tamed, and she has many uses.\n\n§eCombat§r\n· Right-click her while holding any sword, spear, bow or crossbow — she equips that weapon and enters combat. The weapon she was holding drops at her feet, so pick it up.\n· Spears are used as melee thrusts and cannot be thrown.\n\n§eCooking§r\n· Right-click while holding raw food → cooking mode; she cooks continuously.\nSneak + right-click to take the finished food.\n· Note: while idle and empty-handed, she also cooks raw food found in her inventory on her own.\n\n§eFeeding bread§r\n· Right-click while holding bread → she eats it. Works in any state: sitting, fighting, gathering.\n· For 10 seconds afterwards she gains Strength II, Health Boost VI and Absorption VI, plus one immediate heal.\n· Feeding her before a fight is effectively an extra shield plus extra health — well worth it.\n\n§eFarming§r\n· Right-click while holding an iron hoe → farming mode; she finds nearby farmland and works it herself,\nplanting and harvesting vanilla crops, including multi-block ones such as pumpkins and melons.\n· She can use bone meal, and periodically makes her own bone meal.\n· When she stands on a hopper, items in her inventory feed into it automatically.\n\n§eGathering§r\n· Right-click while holding a pickaxe → mining; holding an axe → chopping. She finds nearby ore or logs and walks over to dig.\n· Drops go into her inventory automatically (anything that does not fit drops at her feet).\n· To collect: just right-click (no sneaking needed) to open her inventory.\n· To stop: sneak + right-click → she stops, leaves gathering mode and hands the tool back.\n· Chopping fells the whole connected trunk (up to 96 blocks).\n· Note: she routes around lava and deep pits; if she truly cannot reach a spot she waits there rather than breaking blocks.\n\n§eArmor / Shield§r\n· While empty-handed and idle, right-click her with armor or a shield → she puts it on (note: a shield cannot be equipped while empty-handed).\n· To remove armor: sneak + right-click while holding Maid Command → the armor and shield are handed back to you.\n\n§eOpening her inventory§r\n· While empty-handed and idle, sneak + right-click to open her inventory.\n· She is holding something → a plain right-click opens it.
fictoria.manual.ch3.title=§lChapter 3  Armory Maid
fictoria.manual.ch3.body=§ePromotion§r\n· While empty-handed and idle, right-click while holding "War Cross" → promoted to Armory Maid.\n\n§eSwapping weapons§r\nRight-click while holding a module to swap:\n· Module-M4A1: switches to an M4A1 rifle, high rate of fire\n· Module-GLOCK: switches to a Glock pistol, can reveal hidden enemies\n· Module-MOSSBERG: switches to a Mossberg shotgun, close-range area attack\n· Module-AWP: switches to an AWP sniper rifle, can hit enemies at extreme range\n· Module-SWORD: switches to a Phantoria beam sword, close-range area attack\nThe old weapon drops at her feet.\n\n§eRestrictions§r\n· In armory form she cannot wear armor, nor use vanilla weapons, raw food or hoes — only gun modules.\nTo have her wear armor, cook or farm, revert her to ordinary form first.\n\n§eDemotion§r\n· While empty-handed, right-click while holding "Gentle Cross" → back to ordinary maid.\nEverything on her body and in her inventory drops at her feet — remember to pick it up.
fictoria.manual.ch4.title=§lChapter 4  Extra Features
fictoria.manual.ch4.body=§eMaid Command§r\n· You get one when you tame her. Hold it, or put it in her inventory, and she follows you.\n\n§eLighting§r\n· Put a torch in any of her inventory slots and the maid glows!\n\n§eSaddle§r\n· Put a saddle in her saddle slot → you can ride the maid.\n· Right-click her while holding a saddle → pick her up or put her down.\n\n§eRiding vehicles§r\n· Turn on the "Ride" switch in the command menu and she mounts horses, donkeys, pigs and llamas within 16 blocks;\nin follow mode she drives it after you.\n· If the mount gets stuck on terrain (about 1.5 s without moving) and there is a step ahead, the mount is teleported to you\nand she comes along; if it is more than 40 blocks away it also teleports once.\n· She boards your boat on her own; in follow mode she rows after you —\nall wooden boats, bamboo rafts and boats with chests are supported.\n· In follow mode, if she is more than 38 blocks from you she is teleported back. This does not apply while she is on a vehicle —\nthe vehicle is teleported instead, so she is not pulled off her mount.\n\n§eTactical orders§r\n· Sneak + left-click her → command menu: Follow / Wander / Patrol home\n· Follow mode: follows you like a vanilla cat or dog, and teleports to you when too far.\n· Wander mode: she roams freely with no restrictions.\n· Patrol home mode: she patrols within 36 blocks of the block she is standing on, and teleports back to the centre when she leaves that range.
fictoria.manual.ch5.title=§lChapter 5  Phantoria Ball
fictoria.manual.ch5.body=The Phantoria Ball is a maid's portable home.\n\n§eRecall§r\n· Right-click her while holding an empty green ball → she is stored inside.\nHer 36 inventory slots, worn equipment, name and health are all saved.\n\n§eRelease§r\n· Right-click a block while holding a filled ball → she appears on the block surface.\nThere is a 5-second cooldown after placing, and the ball shows as CD.\n\nNote: a maid wearing armor or a shield has them moved into her inventory when re-placed from a ball.\n\n§eOwner lock§r\n· The ball records its owner. Anyone else who picks it up cannot release her.\nA newly crafted ball has no owner recorded — whoever releases her becomes her owner.
fictoria.manual.ch6.title=§lChapter 6  Crafting
fictoria.manual.ch6.body=Maids come with a lot of related items — do not mix them up!\n\n§eHeart / Card_1§r\nEmerald ×3\n\n§ePhantoria Ball (empty)§r\nEmerald ×8 + Card ×1 (≈ Emerald ×11)\n\n§eMaid Spawn Egg§r\nGold Ingot ×4 + Redstone ×1 + Emerald ×1\n\n§eWar Cross§r\nDiamond ×1 + Gold Ingot ×4 + Emerald ×2\n\n§eGentle Cross§r\nRedstone ×1 + Stick ×4 + Gold Nugget ×2\n\n§eModule-M4A1§r\nBlock of Redstone ×1 + Blaze Rod ×1 + Amethyst Shard ×2 + Obsidian ×2\n\n§eModule-GLOCK§r\nStick ×1 + Redstone ×1 + Stone ×1 + Iron Ingot ×1\n\n§eModule-MOSSBERG§r\nBlock of Redstone ×1 + Blaze Rod ×1 + TNT ×2 + Obsidian ×3\n\n§eModule-AWP§r\nBlaze Rod ×1, Amethyst Shard ×2, Obsidian ×1, Spyglass ×1, Block of Iron ×1 + Block of Redstone ×1\n\n§eModule-SWORD§r\nDiamond Sword ×1

